{"id": "q21", "type": "contextual", "lang": "en", "question": "What documents must a student prepare before an Erasmus+ mobility?", "trace": {"retrieved": 20, "after_threshold": 20, "after_length": 20, "after_dedup": 10, "after_per_doc": 8, "retrieval_s": 0.043, "rerank_s": 0.07, "context": 4, "selected": 5, "confidence": "high", "to_llm": 3, "generation_s": 8.427, "total_s": 8.541, "invalid_citations": 0, "translated": false}, "hit@1": 0.0, "recall@1": 0.0, "precision@1": 0.0, "hit@3": 1.0, "recall@3": 1.0, "precision@3": 0.3333333333333333, "hit@5": 1.0, "recall@5": 1.0, "precision@5": 0.2, "hit@10": 1.0, "recall@10": 1.0, "precision@10": 0.1, "hit@20": 1.0, "recall@20": 1.0, "precision@20": 0.08333333333333333, "mrr": 0.5, "ctx_hit": 1.0, "ctx_mrr": 1.0, "ctx_precision": 0.5, "answer": "[1] [3] Students preparing for Erasmus+ mobility must prepare the following documents:\n- Application form, approved and signed only by the Dean of the Faculty. The form can be requested from the international relations officer of the faculty. Download here (documente utile, cerere de participare în concurs).\n- Photocopy of the passport. The passport must be valid for the entire mobility period.\n- Transcript of Records, issued by the faculty secretariat.\n- Letter of motivation in English, addressed to the Selection Committee, stating the main reasons for choosing the mobility, the candidate’s study objectives and the expected results (1–2 pages).\n- Curriculum Vitae in English – Europass format, including a photo.\n- English language certificate – minimum B1 level, according to the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages (CEFR).\n- Preliminary Learning Agreement (LA) for Studies. Candidates should consult the head of their study programme in order to compare and verify the compatibility of the study programmes. The Learning Agreement should be completed preliminarily, without signatures. Download here", "refused": 0.0, "refusal_correct": 1.0, "latency_s": 8.54, "lang_match": 1.0, "low_confidence": 0.0, "invalid_citations": 0.0, "keyword_recall": 0.5, "citation": 1.0}
